Z||000003||Dan||04-15-2000||01:51 AM|||| Personally, I think this was a good thread in that Stumpy makes a great differentation between hot dogging and serious street problems.I don't know what the reference to the previous thread was,but most of us own Fieros for the occassional hot dog.There is always the place and the time, and never a track when you need one.Does petal to the metal to the speed limit in the proper setting make you a wreckless public hazard? Does everyone drive their Fieros like Grandma Moses on a Sunday afternoon? I'm a firm believer in all out performance at the track, but I reserve the unalianable right to hot dog my Fiero at the right time.Lets start a Fieros for Responsible hot dogging club&gt; Happy motoring.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||04-15-2000||08:13 AM||||Stimpy-dude, you're a lighning rod! I learned a while back the hard way that I should try to make a conscientious attempt to ignore controversial subjects. Ok, so I don't always succeed, but at least I stay out of hot water MOST of the time.<P>Ok, I'm going out on a limb and ignoring what I just said. Yes, racing at night on wet roads is stupid. Everyone of us knows that! Ok, let's drop it now, sheesh! Everyone else, make peace and let's move on.<P>I'm sick of all the bickering, whining, and bitching. The only thing it accomplishes is that 1/3 of the folks get mad, 1/3 of the people get their feeling hurt, and the rest of us don't give a bat's guano about it! Flame away, I'll just ignore you!||||reg||1
